+.\" DO NOT MODIFY THIS FILE!  It was generated by help2man 1.49.3.
+.TH DISPARPDFC "1" "October 2026" "disparPDFc 1.0.6" "User Commands"
+.SH NAME
+disparPDFc \- compare two PDF files textually or visually, without a window
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+.B disparPDFc
+[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... \fI\,FILE1 FILE2\/\fR
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+Compare two PDF files without a window, and print the result code
+(see below).
+.PP
+.B disparPDFc
+is
+.BR disparPDF (1)
+always in batch mode: it compares the files without a window, so needs
+no display, and prints the result code.  By default it compares the
+appearance of the pages; it can also compare their words, or their text
+character by character.  Settings such as the zoom, the tolerances and
+the margins to leave out can be given in a file
+.RB ( \-\-settings ),
+in the same format as the
+.BR disparPDF (1)
+configuration file.
+.SH OPTIONS
+.TP
+\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-appearance\fR
+compare the appearance of the pages (the default)
+.TP
+\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-characters\fR
+compare the text character by character
+.TP
+\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-words\fR
+compare the text word by word
+.TP
+\fB\-\-any\-extension\fR
+accept files whose names do not end in .pdf
+.TP
+\fB\-\-language\fR=\fI\,LANG\/\fR
+use the given translation language, e.g., en for
+English, cz for Czech; English is used if there is
+no translation
+.TP
+\fB\-\-debug\fR=\fI\,2\/\fR
+write the text fed to the sequence matcher into
+temporary files (e.g., \fI\,/tmp/page1.txt\/\fP)
+.TP
+\fB\-\-debug\fR=\fI\,3\/\fR
+as \fB\-\-debug\fR=\fI\,2\/\fR, but also with the coordinates, in y, x
+order
+.TP
+\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
+display this help and exit
+.TP
+\fB\-\-version\fR
+output version information and exit
+.SS "Batch mode options:"
+.TP
+\fB\-\-outType\fR=\fI\,0\/\fR
+print only the result code (the default)
+.TP
+\fB\-\-outType\fR=\fI\,1\/\fR
+print the result code and a description
+.TP
+\fB\-\-pages\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
+compare N pages (default all)
+.TP
+\fB\-\-startPage1\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
+start at page N of FILE1
+.TP
+\fB\-\-startPage2\fR=\fI\,N\/\fR
+start at page N of FILE2
+.TP
+\fB\-\-pdfdiff\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
+save the pages that differ, highlighted, to FILE
+.TP
+\fB\-\-xmlResult\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
+write the result, in XML, to FILE
+.TP
+\fB\-\-key\fR=\fI\,KEY\/\fR
+record KEY in the XML result
+.TP
+\fB\-\-settings\fR=\fI\,FILE\/\fR
+read settings (zoom, margins, tolerances, colors,
+etc.) from FILE, in INI format, instead of using
+the defaults
+.TP
+\fB\-\-compareFonts\fR
+also compare the fonts the files use
+.SS "Result codes, printed in batch mode and also the exit status (modulo 256):"
+.TP
+0
+the files are the same
+.TP
+1
+the files differ
+.TP
+2
+the files have different numbers of pages
+.TP
+3
+a start page is beyond the end of its file
+.TP
+4
+a file has fewer pages than \fB\-\-pages\fR asks for
+.TP
+5
+the same file was given twice
+.TP
+6
+the files use different fonts (with \fB\-\-compareFonts\fR)
+.TP
+\fB\-1\fR
+a command line error
+.TP
+\fB\-3\fR, \fB\-4\fR
+FILE1 or FILE2 cannot be read
+.TP
+\fB\-5\fR
+a page cannot be read
+.TP
+\fB\-6\fR, \fB\-7\fR
+the \fB\-\-pdfdiff\fR or \fB\-\-xmlResult\fR file cannot be written
+.PP
+Built with Qt 6.11.2 and Poppler 26.07.0
+License GPLv2+: GNU GPL version 2 or later <https://gnu.org/licenses/gpl.html>
+.SH AUTHORS
+DiffPDF was written by Mark Summerfield (2008\(en2013).  ConfrontaPDF,
+which added batch mode, is a fork of it by Luca Bellonda (2015), and
+disparPDF is a port of that to Qt\~6 by Yuwsuke Kieda (2026).
+.SH EXAMPLES
+.PP
+.RS
+.nf
+$ disparPDFc a.pdf b.pdf
+0
+$ disparPDFc \-\-outType=1 a.pdf c.pdf
+1|documents differ at page: 1
+.fi
+.RE
+.PP
+Compare the words of two files, saving the pages that differ to
+.IR diff.pdf ,
+and a detailed result, in XML, to
+.IR result.xml :
+.PP
+.RS
+disparPDFc \-\-words \-\-pdfdiff=diff.pdf \-\-xmlResult=result.xml \-\-key=run1 a.pdf b.pdf
+.RE
+.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
+https://github.com/yuw/disparPDF/issues
+.SH "SEE ALSO"
+.BR disparPDF (1),
+.BR diff (1)
